From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/31] Fuse the GDN q/k RMS norm with its scale

The gated delta net normalizes q and k as scale(rms_norm(x), 1/sqrt(n)), two
launches per tensor, 60 per token on qwen35moe. Stock's rms_norm_f32 gets a
do_scale flag that applies the scale op's scale and bias in its store, with
the same arithmetic as scale_f32, so the result is bit-exact.

ggml_cuda_can_fuse only accepts patterns it lists, so the matcher calls
ggml_can_fuse and the memory-overlap check directly. Only on with
GGML_CUDA_P60_MMVQ=1; GGML_CUDA_P60_FUSE_NORM_SCALE=0 turns it off.

2x P100: kernel busy -0.11 ms/token, MTP 8-prompt 109.9 -> 110.5 t/s
(+0.5%, two rounds). Wikitext KLD vs fusion off at ub=1: 0, same top 100%;
MTP outputs byte-identical.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
